"022:001 And David spoke to the Lord the words of this song, in the day in which the Lord rescued him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul.",
"022:002 And the song was thus: O Lord, my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer,",
"022:003 my God; he shall be to me my guard, I will trust in him: he is my protector, and the horn of my salvation, my helper, and my sure refuge; you shall save me from the unjust man.",
"022:004 I will call upon the Lord who is worthy to be praised, and I shall be saved from my enemies.",
"022:005 For the troubles of death compassed me, the floods of iniquity amazed me:",
"022:006 the pangs of death surrounded me, the agonies of death prevented me.",
"022:007 When I am afflicted I will call upon the Lord, and will cry to my God, and he shall hear my voice out of his temple, and my cry shall come into his ears.",
"022:008 And the earth was troubled and quaked, and the foundations of heaven were confounded and torn asunder, because the Lord was angry with them.",
"022:009 There went up a smoke in his wrath, and fire out of his mouth devours: coals were kindled at it.",
"022:010 And he bowed the heavens, and came down, and there was darkness under his feet.",
"022:011 And he rode upon the cherubs and did fly, and was seen upon the wings of the wind.",
"022:012 And he made darkness his hiding-place; his tabernacle round about him was the darkness of waters, he condensed it with the clouds of the air.",
"022:013 At the brightness before him coals of fire were kindled.",
"022:014 The Lord thundered out of heaven, and the Most High uttered his voice.",
"022:015 And he sent forth arrows, and scattered them, and he flashed lightning, and dismayed them.",
"022:016 And the channels of the sea were seen, and the foundations of the world were revealed, at the rebuke of the Lord, at the blast of the breath of his anger.",
"022:017 He sent from above and took me; he drew me out of many waters.",
"022:018 He delivered me from my strong enemies, from them that hated me, for they were stronger than I.",
"022:019 The days of my affliction prevented me; but the Lord was my stay.",
"022:020 And he brought me into a wide place, and rescued me, because he delighted in me.",
"022:021 And the Lord recompensed me according to my righteousness; even according to the purity of my hands did he recompense me.",
"022:022 Because, I kept the ways of the Lord, and did not wickedly depart from my God.",
"022:023 For all his judgements and his ordinances were before me: I departed not from them.",
"022:024 And I shall be blameless before him, and will keep myself from my iniquity.",
"022:025 And the Lord will recompense me according to my righteousness, and according to the purity of my hands in his eye-sight.",
"022:026 With the holy you will be holy, and with the perfect man you will be perfect,",
"022:027 and with the excellent you will be excellent, and with the froward you will be froward.",
"022:028 And you will save the poor people, and will bring down the eyes of the haughty.",
"022:029 For you, Lord, are my lamp, and the Lord shall shine forth to me in my darkness.",
"022:030 For by you shall I run as a girded man, and by my God shall I leap over a wall.",
"022:031 As for the Mighty One, his way is blameless: the word of the Lord is strong and tried in the fire: he is a protector to all that put their trust in him.",
"022:032 Who is strong, but the Lord? and who will be a Creator except our God?",
"022:033 It is the Mighty One who strengthens me with might, and has prepared my way without fault.",
"022:034 He makes my feet like hart's feet, and sets me upon the high places.",
"022:035 He teaches my hands to war, and has broken a brazen bow by my arm.",
"022:036 And you have given me the shield of my salvation, and your propitious dealing has increased me,",
"022:037 so as to make room under me for my going, and my legs did not totter.",
"022:038 I will pursue my enemies, and will utterly destroy them; and I will not turn again till I have consumed them.",
"022:039 And I will crush them, and they shall not rise; and they shall fall under my feet.",
"022:040 And you shall strengthen me with power for the war; you shall cause them that rise up against me to bow down under me.",
"022:041 And you have caused my enemies to flee before me, even them that hated me, and you have slain them.",
"022:042 They shall cry, and there shall be no helper; to the Lord, but he hearkens not to them.",
"022:043 And I ground them as the dust of the earth, I beat them small as the mire of the streets.",
"022:044 And you shall deliver me from the striving of the peoples, you shall keep me to be the head of the Gentiles: a people which I knew not served me.",
"022:045 The strange children feigned obedience to me; they listened to me as soon as they heard.",
"022:046 The strange children shall be cast away, and shall be overthrown out of their hiding places.",
"022:047 The Lord lives, and blessed be my guardian, and my God, my strong keeper, shall be exalted.",
"022:048 The Lord who avenges me is strong, chastening the nations under me,",
"022:049 and bringing me out from my enemies: and you shall set me on high from amongst those that rise up against me: you shall deliver me from the violent man.",
"022:050 Therefore will I confess to you, O Lord, amongst the Gentiles, and sing to your name.",
"022:051 He magnifies the salvation of his king, and works mercy for his anointed, even for David and for his seed for ever."
